workedExamples.solution_text:
Angles on the straight line $DBE$ give $x+y+z=180^{\circ}$.

Alternate angles on parallel lines give $\angle BAC=x$ and $\angle BCA=z$. Also, $\angle ABC=y$.

The equal angles are marked below.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (2,3);\coordinate (C) at (4.5,0);\coordinate (D) at (-0.7,3);\coordinate (E) at (4.8,3);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;\draw (D)--(E);
\draw[->] (1.7,0)--(2.2,0);\draw[->] (0.3,3)--(0.8,3);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};\node[above] at (B) {$B$};\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};\node[left] at (D) {$D$};\node[right] at (E) {$E$};
\node at (1.35,2.7) {$x$};\node at (2.03,2.25) {$y$};\node at (2.72,2.7) {$z$};
\node at (0.7,0.35) {$x$};\node at (3.72,0.35) {$z$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Therefore $\angle BAC+\angle ABC+\angle BCA=180^{\circ}$.

